        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Add web agentic offer, cloud execution, tool releases, and project",
        "summary": "The `common` package gains a new module, `web-agentic-offer.ts`, which allows the Cloud worker to build a sponsored run capability from a browser workspace worktree without a local client inspection, while `sponsored-execution-surface.ts` adds `cloud_linux` as a server-assigned execution surface that no client may claim on the wire. The sponsored skill format in `sponsored-skill.ts` extends `path` tools with optional checksummed release archives (pinned by SHA-256, limited to 4 assets per tool) so the web harness can install vendor CLIs, and a new `sponsoredSkillWebRefusal` function blocks skills lacking `linux` or needing already-installed `path` tools from running on web. Additionally, `common/src/desktop-cloud/project-secrets.ts` introduces sealed project-level environment variables that drop into every chat shell, with reserved names (including `FREEBUFF_*` and `NODE_OPTIONS`) rejected to prevent hijacking.",
        "significance": "major",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "New file `common/src/ads/web-agentic-offer.ts` defines `WEB_CAPABILITY_COMMAND` and `cloudSponsoredCapability`; `common/src/ads/sponsored-execution-surface.ts` adds `SPONSORED_CLOUD_EXECUTION_SURFACE` ('cloud_linux') and `SPONSORED_ACCEPT_SURFACES` now includes 'web'; `common/src/ads/sponsored-skill.ts` introduces `SponsoredSkillToolRelease` types for vendor CLI installation; `common/src/desktop-cloud/project-secrets.ts` adds sealed project environment variables.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The specific rollout mechanism for enabling `web` in `SPONSORED_ACCEPT_SURFACES` and the consumer of the new project secrets API are not shown in this diff.",
        "changes": [
          {
            "area": "common/src/ads",
            "what": "New `web-agentic-offer.ts` module and `cloud_linux` execution surface enable browser workspace sponsored runs",
