        "title": "Document db-leak guard preload and test guard rules in testing guide",
        "summary": "The testing documentation in `docs/testing.md` now includes a section describing the `test/setup-db-leak-guard.ts` preload, which provides an instant Postgres error for CI database URLs and remains ahead of `setup-env.ts` to prevent local test timeouts. The updated guide also clarifies that the shared environment fixture removes `FREEBUFF_ADS_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` to prevent real Slack notifications during test runs. These changes document the existing mechanism where leaked database calls fail instantly rather than timing out via reconnect backoff, ensuring local and CI test environments behave consistently.",
